==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|cocur}}

===Etymology===
{{etyl|gmw|ang}} {{m|gem-pro||*kokar-}}, whence also Old Frisian ''[[koker]]'', Old Saxon ''kokar'' (Dutch ''[[koker]]''), Old High German ''[[kohhar|kohhār]]'' (German ''[[Köcher]]''). The origin of the West Germanic word is unknown, but note that a similar word can be found in the Turkic languages meaning "skin bottle", "hose", including Altay [[кӧкӧр]], Kazakh [[көккөр]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈkoker/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m}}

# a [[quiver]] for arrows
# a [[case]], [[container]]
# a [[sheath]]

